msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:16
msgid "Create a flake using the default template:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:22
msgid "List available templates:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:28
msgid "Create a flake from a specific template:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:34
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:36
msgid ""
"This command creates a flake in the current directory by copying the files "
"of a template. It will not overwrite existing files. The default template is "
"`templates#templates.default`, but this can be overridden using `-t`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:41
msgid "Template definitions"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:43
msgid ""
"A flake can declare templates through its `templates` output attribute. A "
"template has the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:46
msgid ""
"`description`: A one-line description of the template, in CommonMark syntax."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:49
msgid "`path`: The path of the directory to be copied."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:51
msgid ""
"`welcomeText`: A block of markdown text to display when a user initializes a "
"new flake based on this template."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:54
msgid "Here is an example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-init.md:56
msgid ""
"```\n"
"outputs = { self }: {\n"
"\n"
"  templates.rust = {\n"
"    path = ./rust;\n"
"    description = \"A simple Rust/Cargo project\";\n"
"    welcomeText = ''\n"
"      # Simple Rust/Cargo Template\n"
"      ## Intended usage\n"
"      The intended usage of this flake is...\n"
"\n"
"      ## More info\n"
"      - [Rust language](https://www.rust-lang.org/)\n"
"      - [Rust on the NixOS Wiki](https://wiki.nixos.org/wiki/Rust)\n"
"      - ...\n"
"    '';\n"
"  };\n"
"\n"
"  templates.default = self.templates.rust;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

